# Customer Churn Prediction Using Machine Learning

## Project Overview
Customer Churn Prediction is a machine learning project that predicts whether a customer is likely to leave a service or continue using it.

The project uses Logistic Regression to classify customers into two categories: Churn (1) and Stay (0).

## Objectives
- Analyze customer information.
- Identify customers who may leave a service.
- Build a machine learning classification model.
- Create a simple web application for predictions.

## Technologies Used
- Python
- Google Colab
- Pandas
- Scikit-learn
- Joblib
- Gradio

## Dataset Description
The dataset contains 12 sample customer records with the following features:
- Tenure months
- Support tickets
- Monthly spend (INR)
- Last login days
- Plan type
- Churned (target variable)

The dataset is synthetic and created for educational purposes.

## Machine Learning Algorithm
**Logistic Regression**

The model predicts:
- 0 – Customer is likely to stay.
- 1 – Customer is likely to churn.

## Model Performance
- Test accuracy: 100%
- Test records: 3

Note: The dataset is very small, so this result does not establish real-world predictive performance.

## Web Application
A Gradio web application allows users to enter customer details and receive churn predictions.

## Project Files
- `customer_churn_dataset.csv` – Dataset
- `customer_churn_model.pkl` – Trained model
- Google Colab notebook – Project implementation

## Conclusion
This project demonstrates how machine learning can be used to predict customer churn and how a trained model can be integrated into a simple web application.

